              "title": "New Patient Preventive Visit",
              "date": "2024-09-10T09:35",
              "author": "PCP",
              "body": "NEW PATIENT, PREVENTIVE\n\nLucas is a 34-year-old man here to set up primary care. Last regular doctor was in his early twenties; no visits since apart from a walk-in for a sinus thing years ago he can't date. Feels well. No complaints today.\n\nPMH: none he knows of. PSH: none.\nMeds: none. No supplements.\nAllergies: NKDA.\nFH: father has a seizure disorder (generalized, on medication for years per pt). Mother healthy. No early heart disease or cancer that he knows of.\nSH: office administrator at a property management company. Shares an apartment with a roommate. Never smoked, does not drink, no recreational drugs. Walks a fair amount, no formal exercise.\n\nROS: negative across systems on the intake form; reviewed.\n\nExam: well appearing. Vitals as charted, BMI about 25. HEENT unremarkable, dentition fine. Neck supple, no thyroid enlargement or nodes. Heart RRR without murmur. Lungs clear bilaterally. Abdomen soft, nontender, no masses. Skin without concerning lesions. Neuro: alert, fluent, CN grossly intact, strength and gait normal.\n\nPHQ-2: 0.\n\nAssessment / plan\n1. Adult wellness exam, healthy 34M. Baseline CBC, CMP, lipids today.\n2. One-time HIV and hep C screening offered and accepted.\n3. No tetanus record; Tdap given in clinic.\n4. Flu and COVID shots once the fall supply is in; nurse visit.\n5. Return yearly, sooner as needed."
            }
