          "documents": [
            {
              "type": "Progress Notes",
              "title": "Post-ED Follow-up",
              "date": "2025-05-14T16:00",
              "author": "PCP",
              "body": "S: Here after the ED visit Saturday for a convulsive seizure at his desk. Read through the outside record. He tells me now that he has had maybe three or four similar spells over the past several years, always alone or asleep, woke up sore and with a bitten tongue and assumed he'd fainted. Didn't bring it up when he joined last fall. Since discharge no events. Taking valproic acid 500 mg twice a day; a bit queasy the first two days, better taking it with food. Lip sore but healing. Has been out of work since Friday; going back Monday.\n\nO: Vitals as charted. Alert, conversant, normal affect. Small healing mucosal laceration lower lip, no infection. Tongue with resolving bruise laterally. Neuro nonfocal: CN intact, strength 5/5 throughout, gait steady.\n\nA/P:\n1. Epilepsy, newly diagnosed in the ED: temporal sharp waves on EEG, recurrent unprovoked events, father with a seizure disorder. Continue valproic acid 500 mg BID. Neurology referral placed here so it goes to the group we use (ED referral not confirmed). Reviewed what to do if a seizure happens and when to call 911; roommate knows.\n2. Driving: no driving until 6 months without a seizure, so not before mid-November at the earliest. He takes the bus to work. Letter for employer offered.\n3. Lip laceration healing well, no care needed.\nRTC after neurology, or sooner with any event."
            }
