          "documents": [
            {
              "type": "Consult Note",
              "title": "Neurology Consultation (outside)",
              "date": "2025-06-20T11:10",
              "author": "neurology",
              "body": "Outpatient neurology, consultation. Date of visit 6/18/2025.\n\nThank you for sending Mr. Becker, a 35-year-old right-handed office administrator, after a generalized convulsion at work on 5/10/2025.\n\nHistory: Several prior unwitnessed nocturnal or solitary episodes over a number of years with post-event soreness and tongue biting, never evaluated. The May event was witnessed by coworkers, about two minutes of bilateral shaking with postictal confusion. No aura he can recall. No febrile seizures, head injury or CNS infection in childhood that he knows of. Father has a generalized seizure disorder.\n\nMedications: valproic acid 500 mg twice daily since 5/11/2025. Mild early nausea, resolved. No tremor, weight change or hair thinning.\nAllergies: no known drug allergies.\nSocial: never smoker, no alcohol, lives with a roommate.\n\nExamination: BP and pulse normal. Alert, attentive, fluent speech. Cranial nerves II-XII intact. Normal bulk and tone, full strength, reflexes 2+ and symmetric, toes downgoing. Finger-nose and gait normal. No tremor.\n\nData reviewed: ED EEG with intermittent temporal sharp waves; prolactin 44 post-event; ED chemistry and counts normal.\nToday: valproate level 74 mcg/mL (trough), hepatic panel and CBC within normal limits.\n\nImpression: epilepsy with recurrent unprovoked seizures and temporal epileptiform discharges.\n\nPlan:\n- Continue valproic acid 500 mg twice daily; level is therapeutic.\n- Seizure precautions and driving restriction per state rules, reviewed again.\n- Keep a seizure diary.\n- Return in 6 months, sooner for any event.\n\nAllergies reviewed: NKDA."
            }
